Changelog: 24-10-2026 10:26:20

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 07:05:00

Added. The owner's third round of remarks (24-10-2026). The three numbered steps with their buttons are a row of
six pills under the introduction, the header pills' size, spread over the window's width in equal parts, what
each is for in large type and what it does under it (owner, after a first look): PCSX2 Install and Uninstall, BIOS Install and Uninstall (new:
it takes a dump out of PCSX2's bios folder with the files beside it, after a question, and PCSX2 uses another
dump when there is one), Games Add folder and Remove folder; the state of each (PCSX2, the BIOS, the game folders)
stands in a line below; the game folders' line no longer says that subfolders are searched (the wiki does). A Play
time box in the header: the time spent in all games together as PCSX2 counts it (inis/playtime.dat), each game's
time and when it was last played in the tip (owner, 24-10-2026); the BIOS box went from the header (the BIOS
line says which dump PCSX2 uses), the header's pills spread over the window's width in equal parts, as the action
pills do, and the states beside the title (Ready, the controller) stand on the right, ending at the middle of
the last pill. The header boxes are PCSX2 version, Your games, Available in Steam and Play time, and the Games
tab is Your games (owner, 24-10-2026). The tabs' page has no frame around it any more (the
table and the log have their own), and the tabs are the pills' size, the chosen one filled blue. The controller's
state beside the title (owner, 24-10-2026, after a controller switched off by its idle timer left a game without
one): Controller connected (the names in the tip) or No controller, with what to do, read from the kernel's list
of input devices (controllers.py, the run wrapper's rule: a joystick that is not Steam's virtual one) every three
seconds. The run wrapper's log line says whether a controller was there, and when Steam starts a game without one
it says so in a desktop notification (notify-send, where there is one). The introduction's link to the manual is called
Wiki, as everywhere in the suite. The Refresh pill and the new ones keep the blue
left edge only, also under the mouse (a blue tint says they can be clicked), no border all round. The introduction
links to PCSX2's release notes; the PCSX2 line no longer does. The games table's columns are In Steam, Game title,
Id, Type, File name and Screen setting (last, after a look at it), and every choice box in the window is flat,
outlined like the buttons on a see-through background, with a thin chevron (arrow-down.svg in the package) in
place of the old-style drop-down. The Settings tab's boxes stood over each other (the Sound box lay on the
Picture box and hid its lower rows): the Picture box is on the left, the three others under each other on the
right. New settings: Blending accuracy, Video (FMV) shape, No-interlacing patches, and Quit a game with Select +
Start, which binds PCSX2's shutdown to the first controller's Back and Start together ([Hotkeys] ShutdownVM) and
turns PCSX2's question before shutting down off; on by default (owner, 24-10-2026, after trying it on the board):
the app sets it with PCSX2's other settings while PCSX2.ini has no ShutdownVM line, and the switch's off leaves the
line empty, which PCSX2 reads as no binding, so off stays off. The Memory cards tab's picture and
details stand in a box of the picture's width with room around the text. The log says more about the games: the
run wrapper writes the game started (by its file's name, from Steam or a terminal) into the app's log, and the
window sums up PCSX2's own log of its last run once, the next time it looks: the game (named from the catalog),
how long it was played (PCSX2's count, or about the log's last time stamp when PCSX2 did not shut down by itself),
until when and with which controller. The wiki says Steam's overlay takes and shares screenshots (F12, or Steam +
R1 in Big Picture Mode). From the owner's screenshots, after: the Memory cards tab is a block of 720 px at most on
the left, not the window's width; its box shows the icon at 96 px, only while the card has a save, and without the
save's folder (it is in the table, and it was cut off); the Covers dialog says Update Steam, not Update Game Mode,
and wraps its text at a readable width (core). Tests: the pills, the BIOS removed, the column names, the boxes' places, the new
settings and the quit switch, the last run logged once, the wrapper's log line (also in the installer test), and
PCSX2's log read.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 05:06:10

Breaking. Everything about PCSX2 is done in the app (owner, 24-10-2026, after the second round from scratch on the
board): the Play button and the PCSX2 settings button are gone, a game is started from Steam and PCSX2's own window
is not opened, and the nightly channel is gone with its checkbox, its GitHub lookup and its portal notice (the app
installs the stable release it was tried with and nothing else; a notice from before is cleared). The window has
four tabs under the steps: Games (the table, Steam artwork… and Update Steam), Settings, Memory cards and Log.
Settings holds PCSX2's settings that matter for playing, each written into PCSX2.ini the moment it changes and
never while PCSX2 runs: the renderer, the internal resolution, texture and anisotropic filtering, FXAA, integer
scaling, VSync and Show FPS; fast boot and cheats; the volume; vibration and player 2 on the second controller
(SDL-1, the same buttons as player 1). A value PCSX2 holds that the app does not offer is shown as it is. The
Memory cards window is the Memory cards tab, with a Slot choice that puts the chosen card in slot 1 or 2 or takes
it out (a card is in one slot at most), written in PCSX2.ini; before, the slot was set in PCSX2's own window. The
app owns one more setting: the mouse pointer hidden over a full-screen game ([UI] HideMouseCursor). The app has a
log (core's new applog): everything it said and did, with the time, in the Log tab and in
~/.local/share/bc250-pcsx2-manager/bc250-pcsx2-manager.log (1 MB, three older kept); install.sh --uninstall keeps
it, --purge removes it, and the installer test checks both. Refresh is a pill in the header, as in Suite Releases.
The BIOS step shows the dump's name and the Game folders step the folders' names, the paths in their tooltips; the
File column shows the image's name the same way. "What is in it" is "PCSX2's release notes". Steam's full-screen
mode is called Big Picture Mode in the texts (Game Mode is the handheld's session); the Update Steam tooltip in that
session says so. Tests: the tabs, the Settings tab on the defaults and on a file, player 2, the slot, the log tab,
the names without paths, the buttons gone; the nightly tests went with the channel.

Changelog: 23-10-2026 23:12:53

Added. The app sets PCSX2 up, so a game started from Steam goes straight into the game (owner, 23-10-2026: the
emulator only runs the game, the manager does the rest; found in a round from scratch on the board). While PCSX2 is
installed and not running, the app keeps in PCSX2.ini: the setup wizard done, PCSX2's own update check off (it would
replace the pinned build), the BIOS chosen in the app, and player 1 on the first controller (SDL-0, the buttons by
their places as PCSX2's Automatic Mapping binds them; PCSX2 itself maps only the keyboard, so a controller did
nothing in a game). A mapping made in PCSX2's window stays: player 1 is left alone once a controller is bound to it.
Without a PCSX2.ini the app starts from PCSX2 2.8.2's own defaults (pcsx2_defaults.ini, the file PCSX2 wrote at its
first start on the board, without the window's places, the BIOS and the game folder), since PCSX2 asks to reset a
file without its settings version and only its reset writes the hotkeys such as Esc for the pause menu. Every other
line of PCSX2.ini stays as it is. Choose BIOS… replaces Open folder: it copies the chosen dump, with the files beside
it under the same name, into PCSX2's bios folder and makes it the one PCSX2 uses, without a Refresh. A game is named
as PCSX2's catalog names it (GameIndex.yaml, taken out of the AppImage beside it at install, and when the window
opens for a PCSX2 installed before), else by its file's name without a serial in it ("SLUS_215.53.Lumines Plus" is
"Lumines Plus"); the name in Steam follows, and so does the SteamGridDB lookup, which found nothing for a file's name
with a serial in it. A new Screen column sets per game how it fills the screen: Original, Widescreen (PCSX2's
widescreen patch, offered when patches.zip has one for the game) or Fill screen (stretched), kept in the game's own
settings in PCSX2 (gamesettings/<serial>_<CRC>.ini); the CRC is the boot program's, computed as PCSX2 does
(93262D20 for Lumines Plus, as PCSX2 logged it). Update Game Mode is now Update Steam, Covers… is Steam artwork…, and
the In Game Mode box and column are In Steam; the first step says it installs the stable release the app was tried
with, the game folders step that subfolders are searched five deep. Tests: the settings on a first start and on an
existing file, a mapped controller left alone, the BIOS choice, the titles, the patches looked up as PCSX2 does, the
CRC, the screen per game, nothing written while PCSX2 runs, and the catalog taken out at install.

