Release 0.8.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:10:06

Added. Pictures from SteamGridDB for the games in Steam (owner, 22-10-2026), with core's covers. A PS2 disc brings
no pictures, so all four were drawn from the app's icon and the game's title. With the suite's SteamGridDB API key,
entered under the new Covers… button (one key for every app of the suite), Update Game Mode first looks each ticked
game up by its title, the file's name without tags such as "(USA)", and takes the cover, the wide picture, the
banner and the logo with the most votes; a picture SteamGridDB does not have stays drawn. What is found is kept in
~/.local/share/bc250-pcsx2-manager/covers under the game's serial, so it is not asked for again; a game in Steam not
yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network stops the lookup with a message and the drawn
pictures are used; the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key nothing changes. The artwork is now drawn in
the background job, after the lookup. install.sh --uninstall --purge removes the covers folder too; the installer test checks it. Test: the pictures in place of the drawn ones for a file named
"Gran Turismo 4 (USA) (v2.00).iso", and Covers… with Update Game Mode in the window asking for all four kinds,
SteamGridDB's answers made in the test.

